  "about": [
    "Right now I lead observability for a major application rebuild at Northwestern Mutual. The legacy and rebuilt stacks run side by side, and the monitoring has to referee between them fairly or the comparison is worthless. I defined the SLI framework the stakeholders signed off on, and moved measurement to the gateway instead of trusting what each application reports about itself.",
    "Before that I was a core engineer on straight-through processing of insurance applications: 16 Node microservices, 3 React apps, an event-driven architecture on AWS. I took the team's DevSecOps role cause someone had to, and it turned out I liked the pipelines as much as the product. PagerDuty on-call too. You should carry the pager for what you build though.",
    "Nine years in software, seven of them building and operating production web systems in the US, across financial services, healthcare and retail supply chain."
  ],
  "story": [
    {
      "heading": "Started in the pixels.",
      "text": "Years of shipping interfaces people actually touch. The label that stuck at work is frontend guru, though these days the pixels are only half the job."
    },
    {
      "heading": "Then the stack underneath.",
      "text": "Backend, cloud, pipelines, security. Each layer cause the one above it kept breaking on something I couldn't see yet."
    },
    {
      "heading": "Averages hide the users who are waiting.",
      "text": "The distribution has a tail, and the tail is where the experience actually happens. p95 says someone is hurting. p99 says who."
    },
    {
      "heading": "One keystroke. 300 re-renders.",
      "text": "A form-heavy enterprise app cloned its whole state tree on every keystroke. Each of those re-renders is a component doing pointless work."
    },
    {
      "heading": "Rewrite the state layer and it's one.",
      "text": "Instrumented numbers, not an estimate. INP 426ms \u2192 268ms"
    },
    {
      "heading": "Now the platform under all of it.",
      "text": "Kubernetes, Vault, Terraform, the release trains. I run what I build, and I carry the pager for it."
    },
    {
      "heading": "Faster in the field.",
      "text": "A controlled experiment proved which change did it. Making it fast is half the job. Proving why is the half people skip."
    }
  ],
